        60.45355987548828,
        563.0435180664062,
        76.48548126220703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Conditional Diffusion Models",
      "bbox": [
        196.3330078125,
        88.34857940673828,
        415.6690979003906,
        104.38050079345703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ziyu Wan and Lin Zhao",
      "bbox": [
        247.45201110839844,
        116.3888931274414,
        356.876708984375,
        126.1861572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Abstract—This paper proposes DiffPF, a differentiable par-",
      "bbox": [
        58.92701721191406,
        165.8482208251953,
        300.0245361328125,
        173.9090118408203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ticle filter that leverages diffusion models for state estimation",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        175.8112335205078,
        300.0231628417969,
        183.8720245361328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in dynamic systems. Unlike conventional differentiable particle",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        185.77320861816406,
        300.0231628417969,
        193.83399963378906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "filters, which require importance weighting and typically rely",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        195.73622131347656,
        300.023193359375,
        203.79701232910156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on predefined or low-capacity proposal distributions, DiffPF",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        205.6981964111328,
        300.0232849121094,
        213.7589874267578
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "learns a flexible posterior sampler by conditioning a diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        215.6612091064453,
        300.0231628417969,
        223.7220001220703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model on predicted particles and the current observation. This",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        225.6242218017578,
        300.0232238769531,
        233.6850128173828
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "enables accurate, equally-weighted sampling from complex, high-",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        235.58619689941406,
        300.02325439453125,
        243.64698791503906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dimensional, and multimodal filtering distributions. We evaluate",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        245.54920959472656,
        300.0232849121094,
        253.61000061035156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "DiffPF across a range of scenarios, including both unimodal",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        255.51222229003906,
        300.0232238769531,
        263.572998046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and highly multimodal distributions, and test it on simulated",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        265.47418212890625,
        300.023193359375,
        273.53497314453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as well as real-world tasks, where it consistently outperforms",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        275.43719482421875,
        300.0232238769531,
        283.49798583984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "existing filtering baselines. In particular, DiffPF achieves a 90.3%",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        285.40020751953125,
        300.0231628417969,
        293.46099853515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "improvement in estimation accuracy on a highly multimodal",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        295.3622131347656,
        300.0232238769531,
        303.42303466796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "global localization benchmark, and a nearly 50% improvement",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        305.3252258300781,
        300.0232849121094,
        313.38604736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on the real-world robotic manipulation benchmark, compared",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        315.2882385253906,
        300.02325439453125,
        323.34906005859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to state-of-the-art differentiable filters. To the best of our",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        325.250244140625,
        300.0232238769531,
        333.31103515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "knowledge, DiffPF is the first method to integrate conditional",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        335.2132568359375,
        300.0231018066406,
        343.2740478515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion models into particle filtering, enabling high-quality",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        345.1752624511719,
        300.023193359375,
        353.236083984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "posterior sampling that produces more informative particles and",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        355.1382751464844,
        300.023193359375,
        363.1990966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "significantly improves state estimation. The code is available at",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        365.1012878417969,
        300.0232849121094,
        373.162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "https://github.com/ZiyuNUS/DiffPF.",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        375.06329345703125,
        188.09564208984375,
        383.12408447265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Index Terms—Differentiable particle filtering, diffusion mod-",
      "bbox": [
        58.92701721191406,
        391.2622985839844,
        300.02447509765625,
        399.3231201171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "els, Bayesian state estimation, visual odometry, generative models.",
      "bbox": [
        48.96401596069336,
        401.2253112792969,
        300.0232238769531,
        409.2861328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "I. INTRODUCTION",
      "bbox": [
        135.6190185546875,
        436.2174987792969,
        213.37522888183594,
        445.1240539550781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        455.7374267578125,
        67.97132110595703,
        481.35595703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "STIMATING the hidden state of a dynamic system",
      "bbox": [
        69.46501922607422,
        455.4945068359375,
        300.01953125,
        464.40106201171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "from partial and noisy observations is a core challenge",
      "bbox": [
        69.46501922607422,
        467.4494934082031,
        300.01947021484375,
        476.3560485839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "across a wide range of applications. Kalman filters and their",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        479.40447998046875,
        300.02154541015625,
        488.31103515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "extensions [1] have long served as standard tools within",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        491.3604736328125,
        300.0214538574219,
        500.26702880859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the Bayesian filtering framework. However, their reliance on",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        503.3154602050781,
        300.021484375,
        512.2220458984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "linearity and Gaussian noise assumptions severely limits their",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        515.2704467773438,
        300.021484375,
        524.177001953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "applicability to real-world systems that are often nonlinear,",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        527.2254638671875,
        300.02154541015625,
        536.1320190429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "high-dimensional and exhibit multimodal behaviors.",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        539.180419921875,
        261.5359802246094,
        548.0869750976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An alternative line of work, particle filters, avoids these",
      "bbox": [
        58.92702102661133,
        551.8334350585938,
        300.0219421386719,
        560.739990234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "restrictive assumptions by representing the posterior distribu-",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        563.7884521484375,
        300.0214538574219,
        572.6950073242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion with a set of weighted samples instead of relying on",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        575.743408203125,
        300.021484375,
        584.6499633789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "closed-form expressions. Bootstrap particle filter [2], one of",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        587.6984252929688,
        300.0215759277344,
        596.60498046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the most commonly used algorithms, draws particles from",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        599.6534423828125,
        300.0215148925781,
        608.5599975585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the transition model and assigns weights based on observa-",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        611.6094360351562,
        300.021484375,
        620.5159912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion likelihoods. Rao-Blackwellized particle filter [3] further",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        623.564453125,
        300.02154541015625,
        632.4710083007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "improves efficiency by analytically marginalizing part of the",
      "bbox": [
        48.964019775390625,
        635.5194091796875,
        300.0215148925781,
        644.4259643554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
